    {
      "id": "14065986-b52d-41db-aebe-7b9698d1e395",
      "name": "Convert to Binary Data",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        1040,
        656
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const items = $input.all();\n\nreturn items.map(item => {\n  return {\n    json: {\n      chunk_filename: item.json.chunk_filename || 'chunk.pdf',\n      chunk_number: item.json.chunk_number,\n      total_chunks: item.json.total_chunks,\n      source_name: item.json.source_name\n    },\n    binary: {\n      data: {\n        ...item.binary.data,\n        fileName: item.json.chunk_filename\n      }\n    }\n  };\n});"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "5a61de59-ce7b-4487-9cb6-39ccb4d4e5b6",
      "name": "Build chunk file name",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "position": [
        624,
        656
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "const items = $input.all();\nconst results = [];\n\nitems.forEach(item => {\n  const urls = item.json.urls || [];\n  const sourceName = item.json.name || 'document.pdf';\n  const baseName = sourceName.replace('.pdf', '');\n\n  urls.forEach((url, idx) => {\n    results.push({\n      json: {\n        chunk_url: url,\n        chunk_number: idx + 1,\n        total_chunks: urls.length,\n        source_name: sourceName,\n        chunk_filename: baseName + '_part' + \n                        String(idx + 1).padStart(3, '0') + \n                        '.pdf'\n      }\n    });\n  });\n});\n\nreturn results;"
      },
      "typeVersion": 2
    },
    {
      "id": "5138fccf-502e-4ffa-b645-10dfa7a90abb",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1648,
        192
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 672,
        "height": 640,
        "content": "Quick Overview:\nThis workflow manually pulls PDF files from a Google Drive folder, uses PDF.co to detect page counts and split each PDF into 20-page chunks, then uploads the resulting chunk PDFs to a target Google Drive folder.\n\nHow it works?\n- Starts when you manually execute the workflow in n8n.\n- Searches Google Drive for a specific source folder and lists the files inside it.\n- Downloads each file from Google Drive and uploads it to PDF.co to obtain a hosted file URL.\n- Requests PDF metadata from PDF.co to get the total page count and builds a pages list that splits the PDF into 20-page ranges.\n- Calls the PDF.co split endpoint to generate a set of chunk PDF URLs for the specified page ranges. E.g.: For a file of 100 pages it would split into fileName_1, fileName_2, fileName_3, fileName_4, fileName_5\n- Downloads each chunk PDF from PDF.co, assigns a numbered filename based on the original document name, and uploads the chunk files to a Google Drive output folder.\n\nCustomizable: \n- The input and output folder names can be modified as per your requirement\n- The chunk size is customizable, the Google drive can be replaced with OneDrive node\n\nSetup:\n- Add Google Drive OAuth2 credentials and set the source and destination folder IDs for the search and upload steps.\n- Add a PDF.co API credential and ensure your PDF.co workspace allows file upload, info, and split operations.\n- Adjust the chunk size in the splitting logic (default 20 pages) if you want different page ranges per output file."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
